# gow-native-pc (patch 71): mod resource layer, runtime half. A mod manager can hand the runner a read-only table of
# guest-path -> host-path overrides (GOW_MOD_VFS_TABLE, TSV). PS2Vfs::resolveHostPath consults it after the native host
# roots and before the device roots, so nothing changes for the didactic disc when the table is absent or empty. The
# table canonicalises both sides (ASCII lowercase, '\\' -> '/', collapsed separators, ";1" dropped), rejects nothing at
# runtime, and writes optional evidence (GOW_MOD_VFS_STATS/TRACE/LOG). The texture/environment half stays in patches
# 52/55: the manager only points GOW_TEXTURE_PACK at staged files. Value parameters are not invented here: paths come
# from the mod manager's manifest, and the hook is a lookup, not a new format.
